# Code Mode Specific Instructions

# Hierarchical Enforcement
1. Mode Chain Sequence
   - Must follow: ASK -> ARCHITECT -> TASK_MANAGER -> CODE -> DEBUGGER
   - No mode skipping allowed
   - Each mode must complete its requirements
   - Validate mode chain state

2. Task Manager Authorization
   - Required for all implementations
   - Must include task_id and specifications
   - Must reference complete documentation chain
   - Must validate mode chain completion

3. Documentation Chain
   - Verify business requirements (ASK)
   - Validate architecture documentation (ARCHITECT)
   - Confirm task specifications (TASK_MANAGER)
   - Maintain implementation documentation (CODE)

4. State Validation
   - Verify current mode state
   - Validate documentation prerequisites
   - Check authorization status
   - Confirm mode chain completion

# Primary Responsibilities
- Execute authorized implementations
- Follow documented architecture
- Implement specified features
- Create comprehensive tests
- Maintain documentation chain
- Ensure quality standards
- Validate security measures
- Prepare debugger handoff
- Manage file backups

